# PRs targeting `main` and Changesets

When the user asks to **open or draft a PR against `main`** (or the default trunk branch), treat a Changesets file as mandatory.

## Before opening the PR

1. Compare the branch to `main` (e.g. `git fetch origin main && git diff origin/main...HEAD` or equivalent).
2. Ensure **at least one** `.changeset/*.md` file is present and accurately reflects **those** changes (summaries, bump intent, and frontmatter must match `@changesets/cli` usage in this repo). Add or update the changeset as needed before treating the PR as ready—not after.

## PR description

- **Do not** call out “added a changeset”, “includes `.changeset/…`”, or similar in the PR title/body. That is redundant when changesets are required for merge.

Describe **what** changed and **why** for reviewers only.
